From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:47:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: fix IO domain supplies of NanoPi R2S
 Plus

The NanoPi R2S Plus inherits the IO domain supplies of the NanoPi R2S,
but its board wires two of them differently. VCCIO4 is supplied by
vcc_io_33 because the RTL8211F runs its RGMII interface at 3.3 V, and
VCCIO6 is supplied by vcc_18 for the M.2 Wi-Fi slot.

Describe the actual supplies, so the GMAC pins are no longer configured
for 1.8 V while being powered from 3.3 V.

Fixes: b8c028782922 ("arm64: dts: rockchip: Add DTS for FriendlyARM NanoPi R2S Plus")
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s-plus.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s-plus.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s-plus.dts
@@ -46,3 +46,8 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+&io_domains {
+	vccio4-supply = <&vcc_io_33>;
+	vccio6-supply = <&vcc_18>;
+};
